@api = http://localhost:4000/api

### Register an organizer (note the messy email)
POST {{api}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Test Organizer", "email": "  Me@Example.TEST ", "password": "password123", "role": "organizer" }

### Same email again: expect 409
POST {{api}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Someone", "email": "me@example.test", "password": "password123", "role": "attendee" }

### Bad input: expect 422 with four details
POST {{api}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "X", "email": "nope", "password": "short", "role": "admin" }

### Broken JSON: expect 400
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email":

### Log in
# @name login
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "me@example.test", "password": "password123" }

### Wrong password: expect 401
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "me@example.test", "password": "not-my-password" }

### Who am I? (send "Log in" first)
GET {{api}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}

### No token: expect 401
GET {{api}}/auth/me

### Fake token: expect 401
GET {{api}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer abc

########## Events and venues (run npm run seed first, then send these top to bottom)

### Log in as the seeded organizer
# @name org
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "organizer@eventhub.test", "password": "password123" }

### Log in as the second organizer
# @name org2
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "organizer2@eventhub.test", "password": "password123" }

### Log in as an attendee
# @name att
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "attendee@eventhub.test", "password": "password123" }

### Upcoming events, page 2, 5 per page
# @name list
GET {{api}}/events?page=2&size=5

### One event
GET {{api}}/events/{{list.response.body.$.items[0]._id}}

### All venues
# @name venues
GET {{api}}/venues

### Create an event as an organizer: expect 201
# @name created
POST {{api}}/events
Authorization: Bearer {{org.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Test Gig", "description": "Made from REST Client", "startsAt": "2027-01-10T18:00:00Z", "price": 7.5, "venue": "{{venues.response.body.$[0]._id}}", "categories": ["Music", " Food "] }

### The same as an attendee: expect 403
POST {{api}}/events
Authorization: Bearer {{att.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Nope", "startsAt": "2027-01-10T18:00:00Z", "price": 0, "venue": "{{venues.response.body.$[0]._id}}" }

### Invalid input: expect 422 with four details
POST {{api}}/events
Authorization: Bearer {{org.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "ab", "startsAt": "2000-01-01", "price": -1, "venue": "123" }

### Edit someone else's event: expect 403
PUT {{api}}/events/{{created.response.body.$._id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{org2.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Hacked" }

### Edit only the title of your own event: expect 200, description unchanged
PUT {{api}}/events/{{created.response.body.$._id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{org.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Test Gig, renamed" }

### Delete it: expect 204
DELETE {{api}}/events/{{created.response.body.$._id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{org.response.body.$.token}}

### Read it again: expect 404
GET {{api}}/events/{{created.response.body.$._id}}

### A malformed id: expect 404 too
GET {{api}}/events/not-an-id

### Delete a venue that has upcoming events: expect 409
DELETE {{api}}/venues/{{venues.response.body.$[0]._id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{org.response.body.$.token}}

########## Registrations (send the three logins above and "All venues" first)

### A fresh event to register for
# @name gig
POST {{api}}/events
Authorization: Bearer {{org.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Registration Test", "startsAt": "2027-02-01T18:00:00Z", "price": 0, "venue": "{{venues.response.body.$[0]._id}}" }

### Register: expect 201
# @name reg
POST {{api}}/events/{{gig.response.body.$._id}}/register
Authorization: Bearer {{att.response.body.$.token}}

### Register again: expect 409 ALREADY_REGISTERED
POST {{api}}/events/{{gig.response.body.$._id}}/register
Authorization: Bearer {{att.response.body.$.token}}

### Cancel: expect 204
DELETE {{api}}/events/{{gig.response.body.$._id}}/register
Authorization: Bearer {{att.response.body.$.token}}

### Cancel again: expect 404 NOT_REGISTERED
DELETE {{api}}/events/{{gig.response.body.$._id}}/register
Authorization: Bearer {{att.response.body.$.token}}

### Register again with 3 tickets: expect 201 and the same _id as before
POST {{api}}/events/{{gig.response.body.$._id}}/register
Authorization: Bearer {{att.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "ticketCount": 3 }

### Seats left went down by 3
GET {{api}}/events/{{gig.response.body.$._id}}

### Attendees, as the owner: expect the attendee with name and email
GET {{api}}/events/{{gig.response.body.$._id}}/attendees
Authorization: Bearer {{org.response.body.$.token}}

### Attendees, as another organizer: expect 403
GET {{api}}/events/{{gig.response.body.$._id}}/attendees
Authorization: Bearer {{org2.response.body.$.token}}

### My registrations
GET {{api}}/me/registrations
Authorization: Bearer {{att.response.body.$.token}}

### Top venues
GET {{api}}/stats/top-venues

### My events, as an organizer: expect counts and remaining seats
GET {{api}}/me/events
Authorization: Bearer {{org.response.body.$.token}}

### My events, as an attendee: expect 403
GET {{api}}/me/events
Authorization: Bearer {{att.response.body.$.token}}

########## Search (send the logins above and "All venues" first)

### A typo in a title word: expect highlight.title "<mark>Jazz</mark> Night in Weibdeh"
GET {{api}}/events/search?q=jaz

### City, lowercase: note the total
GET {{api}}/events/search?city=amman

### City, uppercase: same total
GET {{api}}/events/search?city=AMMAN

### A category, cheapest first: prices never go down
GET {{api}}/events/search?category=music&sort=cheapest

### An empty minPrice is ignored, not treated as 0
GET {{api}}/events/search?minPrice=&maxPrice=20&sort=cheapest

### A date range, soonest first: an event late on November 30 is still included
GET {{api}}/events/search?from=2026-11-01&to=2026-11-30&sort=soonest

### Page 2, 5 per page
GET {{api}}/events/search?sort=soonest&page=2&size=5

### Bad input: expect 400 BAD_QUERY with details for sort and from
GET {{api}}/events/search?sort=random&from=30-11-2026

### A title with HTML in it
# @name xss
POST {{api}}/events
Authorization: Bearer {{org.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Salsa <img src=x onerror=alert(1)> night", "startsAt": "2027-02-01T18:00:00Z", "price": 1, "venue": "{{venues.response.body.$[0]._id}}" }

### Search for it: the organizer's tag comes back escaped, only <mark> is real HTML
GET {{api}}/events/search?q=salsa

### Clean up: delete it, and search forgets it too
DELETE {{api}}/events/{{xss.response.body.$._id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{org.response.body.$.token}}
